# Repository branch and pull-request consolidation

**Date:** 2026-09-11  
**Classification:** repository maintenance and provenance audit  
**Theorem effect:** none by itself  
**Baseline main:** `c7a8615`

This manifest records the branch and pull-request state immediately before the
repository-wide consolidation requested on 2026-09-11. It is an audit record, not a
route map and not a theorem source.

## Input state

- 117 remote topic branches existed in addition to `main`.
- 99 topic branches were not ancestors of `origin/main`.
- Those branches contained 636 commits outside the ancestry of `origin/main`.
- 53 pull requests were open.
- The working tree was clean before consolidation.

## Resolution policy

1. Keep the `c7a8615` theorem hierarchy and route maps as the starting authority.
2. Join all independent topic tips into one merge ancestry so no branch commit is lost.
3. Import branch-added reports and audits as historical, report-level material. Their
   presence on `main` does not promote their claims.
4. Import reproducibility scripts and document their scope in `research/README.md`.
5. Prefer an explicit later correction or audit when several branches contain different
   blobs at one path.
6. Keep `tmp-noop.txt` and the one-line `docs/audits/STACKED_PR_NOTE.md` temporary
   marker out of the final tree. Their commits remain in the merge ancestry, so their
   provenance is not lost. The substantive audit referenced by the marker is retained.
7. Preserve the live Level I status and the Target C C-II gate unless the authoritative
   route map is separately changed under the promotion procedure.

## Content resolution

The branch deltas contained 524 added paths relative to their respective merge bases.
Sixty-three were already present on `main`. Of the 461 paths absent from `main`,
459 substantive paths were retained and two temporary/no-op files were omitted.

Eight paths had more than one branch-tip blob:

- The three Target B phase-stability reports use the later promoted versions already on
  `main`.
- `target_c_cyclic_d1_p1_endpoint_regular_cell_2026-09-09.md` uses correction
  `34bfd8d`, which removes the singleton-block overclaim.
- `target_c_extreme_stress_circuit_cover_2026-09-09.md` uses upgrade `1194f74`.
- `target_c_extreme_stress_sparsification_2026-09-09.md` uses the repaired version
  already on `main`, not the earlier placeholder.
- Target C modules 53 and 54 use the later promoted versions already on `main`.

PRs #139 and #141 relied on a false inference from consecutive intersecting diameter
edges to an Euler trail. The star-run counterexample in their reviews is binding. The
withdrawal and audit history is retained; the claimed path-based phase closures are not
promoted.

